WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.178
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
07's target gives each class of subject

2
00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:08.119
its own issuer, and a
lifecycle platform covers

3
00:00:08.119 --> 00:00:11.362
the issuers that don't renew
their own certificates.

4
00:00:11.362 --> 00:00:16.862
Intune-managed devices get user and device
certificates from Microsoft Cloud PKI

5
00:00:16.862 --> 00:00:22.201
through SCEP, or during the bridge period
from AD CS through the Intune connector.

6
00:00:22.201 --> 00:00:26.262
Intune renews them, so the CLM
platform doesn't manage them.

7
00:00:26.262 --> 00:00:29.288
PIV cards come from a
Federal PKI shared service

8
00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:32.162
provider through the
card management system.

9
00:00:32.162 --> 00:00:36.928
Domain controller, KDC and LDAPS
certificates stay on retained AD CS

10
00:00:36.928 --> 00:00:41.776
with autoenrollment; the platform
watches them but never renews them.

11
00:00:41.776 --> 00:00:43.987
Everything else lands on the platform.

12
00:00:43.987 --> 00:00:48.471
RADIUS and NPS servers, VPN and
Remote Desktop gateways, SQL Server,

13
00:00:48.471 --> 00:00:53.770
internal web servers and appliances get
certificates from the retained AD CS

14
00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:58.173
hierarchy, which becomes a standalone
CA after Active Directory,

15
00:00:58.173 --> 00:01:02.412
requested and renewed through
CyberArk Certificate Manager.

16
00:01:02.412 --> 00:01:08.047
Public-facing TLS comes from a public CA
the agency authorizes in its CAA records,

17
00:01:08.047 --> 00:01:12.588
renewed by the platform, with ACME
where the endpoint supports it.

18
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:14.592
And for the hierarchy itself,

19
00:01:14.592 --> 00:01:19.351
the platform's revocation monitoring
checks CRL and OCSP endpoints.

20
00:01:19.351 --> 00:01:23.076
So the platform's job is simple
to state: it's the system of

21
00:01:23.076 --> 00:01:27.612
record for every certificate Intune
and the PIV system don't manage.

22
00:01:27.612 --> 00:01:33.597
Sources: Book 07, Chapter 04 (issuer
map; certificate lifecycle management),

23
00:01:33.597 --> 00:01:40.171
Chapter 05 (renewal ownership per certificate
class), Chapter 08 (renewal engines);

24
00:01:40.171 --> 00:01:44.587
research brief section 10;
CyberArk 26.1 Installation

25
00:01:44.587 --> 00:01:49.150
and Upgrade Guide (Certificate
Revocation Monitoring).
